lid none;border-bottom-color:windowtext;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-right-color:windowtext;border-right-width:1pt;padding:0mm 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">0.162</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"81\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:60.65pt;border-style:none solid solid none;border-bottom-color:windowtext;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-right-color:windowtext;border-right-width:1pt;padding:0mm 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">0.028</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"81\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:60.65pt;border-style:none solid solid none;border-bottom-color:windowtext;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-right-color:windowtext;border-right-width:1pt;padding:0mm 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">5.748</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"81\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:60.7pt;border-style:none solid solid none;border-bottom-color:windowtext;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-right-color:windowtext;border-right-width:1pt;padding:0mm 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">0.000</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"81\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:60.7pt;border-style:none solid solid none;border-bottom-color:windowtext;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-right-color:windowtext;border-right-width:1pt;padding:0mm 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">0.243</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n  <td width=\"81\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:60.7pt;border-style:none solid solid none;border-bottom-color:windowtext;border-bottom-width:1pt;border-right-color:windowtext;border-right-width:1pt;padding:0mm 5.4pt\">\r\n  <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">0.243</span></p>\r\n  </td>\r\n </tr>\r\n</tbody></table></div><div><br></div><div>Does it mean that second group has 0.295 lower mean for self-concept than the first group, and it has 0.243 higher mean for interest than the first group?</div><div><br></div><div>Since the p-values are 0.000 for both variables, does this means that those mean differences are significant. </div><div><br></div><div>Am I right? or am I looking at wrong values?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you for your help in advance,</div><div><br></div><div>Best, </div><div><br></div><div>Ai</div><div><br></div><div> </div><div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div>"
